16479111020717__567196f2-7644-4439-92dc-9a0910a80564-liquid-1":{"type":"liquid","settings":{"code":"<h2>How Much Ashwagandha Should I Take?<\/h2><p>When starting a Ashwagandha regimen, a good starting dose is <b>125mg<\/b> which is also the recommended dose for our Ashwagandha products. As with any supplement, it's always best to consult with a healthcare professional before starting a new regimen.<\/p>\n<a href=\"https:\/\/nextevo.com\/pages\/how-much-ashwagandha-should-i-take\" class=\"btn btn--secondary\" style=\"background: #002D72; color: #ffffff;\">See Our Ashwagandha Dosage Guide                            <\/a><\/center>","width":"50%","alignment":"center"}},"dosage_chart_gPUEQp":{"type":"dosage_chart","disabled":true,"settings":{"title":"How to Calibrate Your CBD Dosage","image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/dosage-icon.svg","color":"#4057a2","text_1":"Determine your body weight","color_1":"#f5f6fb","text_2":"Start with 1-6mg for every 10lbs of body weight","color_2":"#e4def4","text_3":"Increase dose incrementally by 5-10mg at a time","color_3":"#a7bbe5","text_4":"Keep a journal to track your dosage and its effects","color_4":"#d1e5e7","text_5":"","color_5":"#f5f6fb","width":"50%","alignment":"center"}},"image_6tCtme":{"type":"image","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/stress-cbd-complex-gummies-60-ct-971955.png","enable_size":true,"height":400,"link":"","width":"50%","alignment":"center"}}},"block_order":["template--16479111020717__567196f2-7644-4439-92dc-9a0910a80564-liquid-1","dosage_chart_gPUEQp","image_6tCtme"],"disabled":true,"custom_css":[".image-wrap {background-color: #f9f2ed;}"],"settings":{"id":"","full_width":true,"space_around":true,"margin_top":0,"margin_bottom":0,"padding_around":true,"padding_top":75,"padding_bottom":75,"background":"#f9f2ed","heading_color":"#002d72","text_color":"#0e1111"}},"164191583148ab66dc":{"type":"faq","blocks":{"1641915831d00a823b-0":{"type":"question","settings":{"title":"What does 'THC-free gummies' mean?","text":"<p>THC-free gummies are wellness products that contain no tetrahydrocannabinol (THC), the psychoactive component commonly found in cannabis. This means they provide the benefits of their active ingredients without causing any psychoactive effects, making them suitable for those who want to avoid any alteration in mental state.<\/p>"}},"4794c9ac-ba35-4b34-9fdf-1f354d679cfa":{"type":"question","settings":{"title":"Is CBD still effective without THC?","text":"<p>Yes, CBD can be effective without THC. Many users experience the benefits of CBD, such as relaxation, reduced anxiety, and pain relief, even in the absence of THC. CBD operates on different pathways in the body and does not require THC to exert its therapeutic effects.<\/p>"}},"196b91ac-7a99-4af0-8fc9-b94149815097":{"type":"question","settings":{"title":"Can I fail a drug test?","text":"<p>Using THC Free gummies should not cause you to fail a drug test, as these products do not contain THC, the substance most commonly tested for in drug screenings. However, it's crucial to purchase your gummies from reputable sources that ensure their products are completely free of THC.<\/p>"}},"f0cd3a71-ea8d-4006-a6cf-0927a6976faf":{"type":"question","settings":{"title":"What's the difference between a CBD and THC gummy?","text":"<p>The main difference between CBD and THC gummies lies in their chemical composition and effects. THC gummies contain tetrahydrocannabinol, which can induce psychoactive effects such as euphoria. In contrast, CBD gummies are made with cannabidiol, which does not produce psychoactive effects but is often used for its potential health benefits like reducing inflammation, anxiety, and managing pain. Depending on your needs and the legal status of cannabis in your area, you might choose one type over the other.<\/p>"}}},"block_order":["1641915831d00a823b-0","4794c9ac-ba35-4b34-9fdf-1f354d679cfa","196b91ac-7a99-4af0-8fc9-b94149815097","f0cd3a71-ea8d-4006-a6cf-0927a6976faf"],"settings":{"spacing":t